      "approved": true,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 0,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The two new tests assert the required rejection results, empty text, and zero worker starts; the repeated-reference test also checks the one-page success case. The existing stream-filter tests are present, and the `build-and-gate` job runs `dotnet test AirlineDemo.sln`, which includes them.",
      "findingList": []
    },
    {
      "agentId": "security-reviewer",
      "reviewType": "security",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The new preflight undercounts filtered text sources for supported filter chains, allowing oversized or repeatedly referenced decoded text to reach the worker.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 667,
          "message": "The text-source bound can be bypassed with a filter chain whose first filter is not FlateDecode. Count the fully decoded content length before applying the 512 KiB limit. OWASP A06:2025.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "PreflightPageContentSources calls DecodedContentStreamLength for each referenced page-content stream. When the first filter is not FlateDecode or Fl, that method counts the encoded stream length instead of the decoded text-source length.",
            "failureScenario": "An attacker submits a PDF with a Flate-compressed text stream wrapped in ASCII85. The encoded stream can be under 512 KiB while decoding to more than 512 KiB; repeated page references are then charged only the small encoded length, so the PDF passes the intended text-source bound and can make the worker process far more repeated text than the limit allows."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
